<title>UK: Enel fuel burn drops 300,000 t in Nov from yr ago.</title>
<headline>Enel fuel burn drops 300,000 t in Nov from yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption of low sulphur heavy fuel oil used for power generation in Italy fell by about 300,000 tonnes in November from the same month a year earlier, said industry sources on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Around 1.4 million tonnes of heavy fuel oil with less than one percent sulphur was burnt by state power company Enel last month compared to 1.7 million in November 1995, the sources said.</p>
<p>Total heavy fuel consumption was down to about 1.9 million tonnes from just under 2.2 million in November 1995.</p>
<p>The lower consumption was mostly due to increased burning of gas but also due to more hydro-electric power generation.</p>
